  "about": "Thailand: the Bank of Thailand's financial-institution holidays (yearly notification under the Financial Institution Business Act), NOT the public-holiday list. Since 2007 BOT keeps Asarnha Bucha but not Buddhist Lent Day; it does not take the Royal Ploughing Ceremony or most cabinet 'special' days unless it adds them by separate notice; substitution days are listed one by one because BOT does not substitute consistently (e.g. none for Songkran 2023 or 2025). Branches in 5 southern provinces and Islamic Bank close extra days (not modelled). Fixed dates plus lunar tables plus explicit exceptions; checked against BOT or press reproductions of BOT lists for 2019-2027. Covers 2019-2027 (2027 notification No. 37/2569, 17 Aug 2026); 2010-2018 not verified.",
